1 NOTE @NI14@
0 @NI14@ NOTE
1 CONC Jan and Maria lived in a large one room log house with a la
1 CONC rge stone fireplace and a dirt floor.  This house was tor
1 CONC n down in 1909.  They had a farm of 17 acres.  Šiba is i
1 CONC n a vally between two gently sloping hills.  The Maçus home
1 CONC stead gradually rises from the stream.  There is a small pa
1 CONC tch of flat land where the current two houses are.  To ge
1 CONC t to the houses from the main highway one must cross a brid
1 CONC ge over the stream.  Two Maçus brothers live in two house
1 CONC s on this property, Andrej and Jozef.
1 CONT 
1 CONT Matyus means little Matthew.  The family has passed down th
1 CONC e story of how their name became Maçus as follows:  Origina
1 CONC lly the family name was Kasprik ( this is a Polish name, Ši
1 CONC ba is very close to the Polish border).  The village wher
1 CONC e these Kaspriks lived was overcrowded with Kaspriks and i
1 CONC t was very difficult to distinquish one from another.  On
1 CONC e of our ancestors with the name of Matus (Matthew) began t
1 CONC o be referred to by his first name.  He accepted it as hi
1 CONC s surname and passed it down to later generations.  Due t
1 CONC o illiteracy the name has evolved over the generations to b
1 CONC ecome Maçus.  This is not a Slovak name and tthe only perso
1 CONC ns of this name in Slovakia are our relatives.  There are n
1 CONC o persons of the name Kasprik living in Šiba.
