0 @NI29@ NOTE
1 CONC Karl emigrated 15 May 1888.  He used the name Karl Nojd o
1 CONC n his emigration papers and in the census records.  All oth
1 CONC er official records show his name as Charles Nye.  He was b
1 CONC orn Karl August Karlsson.  He was a soldier and was assigne
1 CONC d the solier name of Nojd.  Some men returned to using thei
1 CONC r birth name when they no longer were soldiers and some kep
1 CONC t their soldier names.  Karl chose to keep using his soldie
1 CONC r name.  In Sweden all soldiers were assigned a short one s
1 CONC yllable name and there was only one soldier of that name i
1 CONC n each district.
1 CONT Karl emigrated without any other family members.  His siste
1 CONC r, Anna,  emigrated 7 August 1887 and was living in Long Is
1 CONC land, New York.  His sister, Hannah, emigrated 25 Februar
1 CONC y 1904. She returned to Sweden 31 December 1915.  His broth
1 CONC er, David, emigrated  13 June 1892 and I was told he live
1 CONC d in Florida and died in prison for counterfeiting money
1 CONC .  Karl's brother, William, lived in Chicago, Illinois fo
1 CONC r a number of years and then he returned to Sweden.
