1 CONC Anna was jailed several times for stealing and misconduct
1 CONC .  She was jailed in 1844, 1846, 1848 and 1849.  After he
1 CONC r husband died in 1850 the children were split up and put i
1 CONC n foster homes.  It is thought that she died between 1851 a
1 CONC nd 1859 because Gustava was married in 1859 and in her marr
1 CONC iage records it states that her parents are dead.
1 CONT Prior to her marriage she was a maid/servant.  Anna was jud
1 CONC ged for petty theivery at Skånstorp in 1844.  She was arres
1 CONC ted for stealing at Ledbäck in 1846.  In 1848 she was punis
1 CONC hed by being fed bread and water - this was the church dut
1 CONC y in 1849.  She was arrested again and taken to Östersund'
1 CONC s Prison in 1849.  She was arrested in Jäntland in 1850 bec
1 CONC ause of a writing from the government office.  Possibly Ann
1 CONC a died in Österlund.  For sure she did not come back to B
1 CONC o Parish.
1 CONT The records in Österlund ,15 Jul 1850, state that Anna wa
1 CONC s born on Löthbergs Parish, Linköping in 1806. She told he
1 CONC r family that she was going to the market but instead she r
1 CONC an off with a man and wandered all over Sweden and Norway w
1 CONC ith him.  They made baskets and sold them and threatened pe
1 CONC ople if they did not buy any.  Anna claims her husband, Olo
