0 @NI326@ NOTE
1 CONC The 1900 Chippewa Co, MI, USA Census lists Harry Hand ag
1 CONC e 8 living with his grandparents, Win and Catherine Hand
1 CONC .  This census report states that Harry was born in mont
1 CONC h 9 and year 91.  The years of birth for his grandparents a
1 CONC re 10 years off.   The 1910 Chippewa Co Census lists Harr
1 CONC y Fisher age 17 living with his grandparents, Win and Cathe
1 CONC rine Hand. This census was taken on 28 April 1910.  This wo
1 CONC uld make Harry's year of birth 1893.   His Mother was neve
1 CONC r married to his father.  She later married Mr Henry Fishe
1 CONC r and I was told by Harry that he was the only one of his m
1 CONC other's 7  husbands to treat him nicely so he took the nam
1 CONC e of Fisher.  Harry served in France during WW I.  He wa
1 CONC s a foreman and purchasing agent for the Wonder Bread Compa
1 CONC ny which was owned by Continental Baking Company.
1 CONT Harry stated his birth was in 1897, but also stated that h
1 CONC e had lied in a lot of records and was confused about his c
1 CONC orrect birth year.  See notes under William Alexander to se
1 CONC e why I think he was born in 1893.  This date is consisten
1 CONC t with the 1910 census records and also the fact that Willi
1 CONC am Alexander suddenly disappears in August 1893 from the mu
1 CONC ster rolls of Fort Brady and the fact that Jennie was divor
1 CONC ced from her husband in January 1894
1 CONT 
1 CONT The 1900 and 1910 census records state that Harry's fathe
1 CONC r is "unknown".  Harry's marriage license to Sylvia state
1 CONC s that his father is "unknown".
