1 NOTE @NI328@
0 @NI328@ NOTE
1 CONC Harry's Mother was never married to his father.  Sylvia Hat
1 CONC haway Hoyt told me that Harry's natural father's surname wa
1 CONC s Alexander.  Jennie worked as a domestic and as a cook.  A
1 CONC ccording to the St James Episcopal Church  Log Book for  18
1 CONC 82 Jennie was confirmed 15 April 1888 and she was residin
1 CONC g and in service at Fort Brady. There was a soldier named W
1 CONC illiam Alexander who was stationed there at the time that J
1 CONC ennie became pregnant with Harry.  William Alexander worke
1 CONC d as a cook and he left suddenly.  There is absolutely noth
1 CONC ing that indicates William Alexander is the father of Harry
1 CONC .  His surname was Alexander and he was in the right plac
1 CONC e at the right time.  I attempted to find some records tha
1 CONC t might provide more details about Jennie's work at Fort Br
1 CONC ady but have been unsuccessful.  I have been told that it w
1 CONC as common practice that if a soldier got a woman pregnant t
1 CONC here would be no official record and he would be quietly sh
1 CONC ipped out.  According to the records of Fort Brady, Willia
1 CONC m enlisted 16 August 1890 for a term of 5 years.  The For
1 CONC t Brady muster rolls show William Alexander went on a 3 mon
1 CONC th furlough 16 Aug 1893.  He never returned and there is n
1 CONC o mention of him anymore.  His military records do not sa
1 CONC y anything except that he was honorably discharged 15 Nov 1
1 CONC 893 with no mention of why he did not serve his full 5 yea
1 CONC r term.  I do not think William became ill as there were ot
1 CONC her soldiers listed in the muster rolls as being in the inf
1 CONC irmary and there is no mention of William Alexander ever be
1 CONC ing in the infirmary.  Harry stated that he was born in 189
1 CONC 7.  According to the 1900 and 1910 census records he shoul
1 CONC d have been born in 1892-1893.  I think he was born in Sept
1 CONC ember 1893 as It is  close enough to the census dates to b
1 CONC e reasonable.  It also fits in with the fact that Jennie ob
1 CONC tained a divorce in Jan 1894.  I have not been able to loca
1 CONC te a divorce decree, but the Sault St Marie Evening News da
1 CONC ted 13 Jan 1894 states that Mrs Jennie Reynolds has obtaine
1 CONC d a divorce.  She probably was divorced in December 1893 o
1 CONC r January 1894.
1 CONT William was 5'5" and Jennie was 6' tall.  Jennie's father
1 CONC , Winn, was 6'5 1/2" tall.  Harry was 5'10" tall.  It is hi
1 CONC ghly unusual for a man to be smaller than his mother.  Ever
1 CONC ything seems to indicate that Harry's father must have bee
1 CONC n small.
1 CONT 
1 CONT There is a William R. Alexander buried in Thomasburg Cemete
1 CONC ry, Hungerford Twp, Hastings Co, Canada.  Also Leola R an
1 CONC d J Earl Alexander.
