0 @NI355@ NOTE
1 CONC I have a copy of William's land records dated  2 July 183
1 CONC 5 when his petition was approved. Vol. 091 pg 029 Ontario 2
1 CONC 8 Oct 1850 V. 002 pg 255, May 1841 & Aug 1845 V025 pg 381
1 CONC . According to these papers William paid John Maguire for a
1 CONC n interest in his land and John Maguire appointed William t
1 CONC o act as his attorney to do everything necessary to secur
1 CONC e the land grant.  I have a copy of the Order in Council da
1 CONC ted 14 Sep 1825 granting John Maguire 200 acres.  I also ha
1 CONC ve a copy of a document dated 25 Aug 1826 in which John Mag
1 CONC uire appoints William Hand as his attorney in all matters r
1 CONC elating to securing the land grant.  This document was witn
1 CONC essed by Richard Bradley.   William obtained the land gran
1 CONC t because John Maguire drowned, in the Welland Canal, the m
1 CONC iddle of May 1830.
1 CONT  William was married twice.  His second wife was named Mar
1 CONC y and she is listed in the Simcoe Co census records of 1861.
1 CONT I believe William also had a daughter named Elizabeth.  H
1 CONC e may have had other children also.
1 CONT The land grant was in concession VI and lot 6.  The villag
1 CONC e of Stanton is on the former Hand farm.
0 @HI355@ NOTE
1 CONC (Research):William's age is unclear.  In the 1861 census h
1 CONC e states he is age 62 which would make him born circa 1799
1 CONC .  In the 1871 census he states he is age 70 which would ma
1 CONC ke him born circa 1801.  The Dundalk Herald Newspaper state
1 CONC s he died in his 85th year and his grave marker stated he d
1 CONC ied at age 88. The official death registration states he wa
1 CONC s age 78 at his death. This information was provided by hi
1 CONC s son, Thomas.  William could have been born anywhere fro
1 CONC m 1789- 1801.  
1 CONT I think 1799/1800 is the most probable date of his birth.
