0 @NI357@ NOTE
1 CONC I believe that the Bradley family came from Castlecomer, Co
1 CONC . Kilkenny, Ireland.  Richard Bradley signed William Hand'
1 CONC s land grant papers as a witness.  The land record index re
1 CONC fers to Richard Bradley of Mulmur Twp and Richard's land gr
1 CONC ant papers, dated 1826, state that he was age 22, single an
1 CONC d from Castlecomer, Co. Kilkenny, Ireland and that he emigr
1 CONC ated June of 1825. There were at least 4 Bradley men that s
1 CONC ettled in Mulmur Twp.  William, Edward, Levi and Richard
1 CONC .  They have birth dates that are estimated from the censu
1 CONC s records to be 1800, 1802, 1804 and 1806.  Also Mulmur wa
1 CONC s a very isolated rural area.  It seems highly probable tha
1 CONC t they were brothers.  There is a reference in the Soo Even
1 CONC ing News which refers to Catherine Hand's Uncle Edward Brad
1 CONC ley.
1 CONT For the land records of  Richard Bradley see:  01 c13 05414
1 CONC 9.  He resided in York.  The land grant was for Lot W 1/2 1
1 CONC 9 conc 1 WHST.  It is an Order in Council dated 9 Nov 182
1 CONC 5 and 20 Nov 1832.
