0 @NI391@ NOTE
1 CONC I have no proof Jane is the daughter of William but I belie
1 CONC ve she is.  William Hand and William Walker were witnesse
1 CONC s at her wedding. Her children's names also fit the Irish n
1 CONC aming pattern for William.  William Hand and William Walke
1 CONC r were the first settlers in Mulmur Twp.  William Hand wa
1 CONC s Anglican and a member of St Luke's Anglican Church of Mul
1 CONC mur.  In the book "Mulmur-The Story Of A Township" on pag
1 CONC e 44 it states that the Misses Elizabeth and Jane Hand too
1 CONC k organ lessons from the wife of one of the early rectors o
1 CONC f St. Luke's.  In the same book there is a cute story on pa
1 CONC ge 18 about the naming of the town of Stanton.  The origina
1 CONC l Hand family farm was where the town of Stanton is now.  T
1 CONC he Hand family wanted the name of the settlement to be Hand
1 CONC ville and the Walker family wanted the name to be Walkervil
1 CONC le.  To avoid a fight the Judge that had the responsibilit
1 CONC y for the final decision said "You're both wrong. It's Stan
1 CONC ton."
