1 CONC I spent some time at his farm in Taloga, OK.  The farm wa
1 CONC s 7 square miles.  Willis showed us around the land.  We sa
1 CONC w cattle drinking at a waterhole and he showed us bars in t
1 CONC he ground that the cattle were afraid to cross.  The cattl
1 CONC e were not fenced in but for some reason they would not cro
1 CONC ss over the metal bars in the ground.  They also had peacoc
1 CONC ks because they eat locusts.  The peacocks were very tame
1 CONC .  My father told me once when he was very young and visiti
1 CONC ng his relatives on the farm there was a locust storm
1 CONC .  A  neighbor woman had on a dress with green polka dots a
1 CONC nd the locusts ate the polka dots out of the dress.
